    {
      "schema_version": 6,
      "book_id": "2TI",
      "chapter": 2,
      "chapter_usfm": "2TI.2",
      "version_id": 2692,
      "version_abbr": "NASB2020",
      "verses": [
        {
          "verse": 1,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.1",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "You therefore, my son, be strong in the grace that is in Christ Jesus."
        },
        {
          "verse": 2,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.2",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "The things which you have heard from me in the presence of many witnesses, entrust these to faithful people who will be able to teach others also."
        },
        {
          "verse": 3,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.3",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Suffer hardship with me, as a good soldier of Christ Jesus."
        },
        {
          "verse": 4,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.4",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "No soldier in active service entangles himself in the affairs of everyday life, so that he may please the one who enlisted him."
        },
        {
          "verse": 5,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.5",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "And if someone likewise competes as an athlete, he is not crowned as victor unless he competes according to the rules."
        },
        {
          "verse": 6,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.6",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "The hard-working farmer ought to be the first to receive his share of the crops."
        },
        {
          "verse": 7,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.7",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Consider what I say, for the Lord will give you understanding in everything."
        },
        {
          "verse": 8,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.8",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Remember Jesus Christ, risen from the dead, descendant of David, according to my gospel,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 9,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.9",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "for which I suffer hardship even to imprisonment as a criminal; but the word of God is not imprisoned."
        },
        {
          "verse": 10,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.10",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "For this reason I endure all things for the sake of those who are chosen, so that they also may obtain the salvation which is in Christ Jesus and with it eternal glory."
        },
        {
          "verse": 11,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.11",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "The statement is trustworthy:For if we died with Him, we will also live with Him;"
        },
        {
          "verse": 12,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.12",
          "line_type": "q",
          "text": "If we endure, we will also reign with Him;If we deny Him, He will also deny us;"
        },
        {
          "verse": 13,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.13",
          "line_type": "q",
          "text": "If we are faithless, He remains faithful, for He cannot deny Himself."
        },
        {
          "verse": 14,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.14",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Remind them of these things, and solemnly exhort them in the presence of God not to dispute about words, which is useless and leads to the ruin of the listeners."
        },
        {
          "verse": 15,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.15",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Be diligent to present yourself approved to God as a worker who does not need to be ashamed, accurately handling the word of truth."
        },
        {
          "verse": 16,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.16",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "But avoid worldly and empty chatter, for it will lead to further ungodliness,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 17,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.17",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "and their talk will spread like gangrene. Among them are Hymenaeus and Philetus,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 18,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.18",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "men who have gone astray from the truth, claiming that the resurrection has already taken place; and they are jeopardizing the faith of some."
        },
        {
          "verse": 19,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.19",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Nevertheless, the firm foundation of God stands, having this seal: “The Lord knows those who are His;” and, “Everyone who names the name of the Lord is to keep away from wickedness.”"
        },
        {
          "verse": 20,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.20",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Now in a large house there are not only gold and silver implements, but also implements of wood and of earthenware, and some are for honor while others are for dishonor."
        },
        {
          "verse": 21,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.21",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Therefore, if anyone cleanses himself from these things, he will be an implement for honor, sanctified, useful to the Master, prepared for every good work."
        },
        {
          "verse": 22,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.22",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Now flee from youthful lusts and pursue righteousness, faith, love, and peace with those who call on the Lord from a pure heart."
        },
        {
          "verse": 23,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.23",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "But refuse foolish and ignorant speculations, knowing that they produce quarrels."
        },
        {
          "verse": 24,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.24",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "The Lord’s bond-servant must not be quarrelsome, but be kind to all, skillful in teaching, patient when wronged,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 25,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.25",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "with gentleness correcting those who are in opposition, if perhaps God may grant them repentance leading to the knowledge of the truth,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 26,
          "usfm": "2TI.2.26",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "and they may come to their senses and escape from the snare of the devil, having been held captive by him to do his will."
        }
      ],
